    "cost_closing_html":  "\u003cp\u003eThat is about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a burrito\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) versus \u003cstrong\u003e$10 or more\u003c/strong\u003e for a ranch chicken burrito at a fast-casual counter. Same flavor, a fifth of the price.\u003c/p\u003e",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eGreek yogurt is the base of the sauce, not sour cream.\u003c/strong\u003e It brings the protein up while it keeps the sauce creamy. Buy the big tub, it costs less per ounce and this recipe uses a lot of it.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eA packet of dry ranch plus a splash of bottled ranch is all the flavor.\u003c/strong\u003e You are not buying a whole bottle of dressing to pour on, just a few spoonfuls stirred into the yogurt, so one bottle lasts a long time.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eTomatoes with green chiles do double duty.\u003c/strong\u003e One can brings the tomato and the mild heat in a single step, so you skip buying both. Drain it well so the burritos hold up in the fridge."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cube the chicken breast and cook it in a skillet with the olive oil over medium-high heat until it reaches 165F inside. Add the taco seasoning and toss to coat.",
                    "Saute the diced yellow onion and red bell pepper until soft, then stir in the drained tomatoes with green chilies and the black beans and warm through.",
                    "Make the ranch sauce: whisk the Greek yogurt, ranch dressing, ranch seasoning mix, sugar, smoked paprika, ground cumin, and cayenne pepper until smooth.",
                    "Combine the chicken with the pepper, tomato, and bean mixture in your pot.",
                    "Warm the tortillas, then fill each with the chicken mixture, a scatter of shredded cheddar, and a spoon of the ranch sauce before you wrap."
                ],
    "portion_html":  "\u003cp\u003eSet the full pot on your scale and subtract the empty-pot weight from Step 1. Divide that total food weight by 14, scoop the same amount into each tortilla, and finish with an even spoon of the ranch sauce. Every burrito lands near {{cal}} calories with {{protein}} grams of protein.\u003c/p\u003e",
